                   <p>
                       Karwa chauth is a day of fast. Married women fast and do not eat food or drink water for whole day.
                        On this day Hindu women offer prayers seeking 
                       the welfare, prosperity, welfare and longevity of their husbands. Karwa Chauth 
                       falls about nine days before Diwali on the Kartik ki chauth sometime in October 
                       or November. He is the most important fast observed by women in northern India. 
                       A woman keeps a fast for the welfare of her husband, who becomes her protector 
                       after she leaves her parents&#39; house. Her husband provides food, shelter, 
                       clothing, respectability, comfort and happiness. This is really very difficult 
                       to fast when a track begins and ends before sunrise to worship the moon, which 
                       usually rises about 20:45 No food or water should be taken after 4 am or after 
                       sunrise. </p>
                    <p>
                        Today, this fast is also seen as a modern educated homes, becoming a symbol of 
                        the feeling that a woman is her husband. One thing to ensure that the Baya reach 
                        his relatives at home, where a girl has done during the day, the night before. 
                        Baya is given in-law after manasna. If the mother-in-law is not present, the 
                        oldest woman of the house is the Baya. Sometimes a parent wants to limit the 
                        perishable, and leave the money and clothes for his mother-in-law. Preparation 
                        for Puja should start around 4 or 5:00 Someone older, who are ready, or 
                        housewife even as the situation demands, prepares a suitable place in the puja 
                        room, where a large room that can accommodate all women who are invited to Baya, 
                        if not the best place is of a veranda or courtyard open, because usually the 
                        weather is not cold during this season. The place is decorated puja Kharia 
                        Matti, which has been soaked in water two to three hours earlier, and takes a 
                        semi-liquid form. A Chowk as in any other puja - is decorated on the floor.</p>
